From 71adcfbaa4363339be2675ba32f47e2538159f53 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GADGETN1K <playgadgetnik@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:29:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stack: a2dp: Encode SBC at 229 kbps by default

On devices whose Wi-Fi and Bluetooth share a 2.4 GHz antenna, busy Wi-Fi
leaves the A2DP link too little airtime for SBC at 328 kbps (bitpool 53):
the TX queue keeps backing up and is flushed, which is heard as dropouts.
Use 229 kbps, the rate already used for non-EDR peers, which needs about
30% less airtime.
---
 system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_sbc_encoder.cc | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_sbc_encoder.cc b/system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_sbc_encoder.cc
index fb7feabe84..03294f2981 100644
--- a/system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_sbc_encoder.cc
+++ b/system/stack/a2dp/a2dp_sbc_encoder.cc
@@ -49,7 +49,7 @@
 #define A2DP_SBC_ENCODER_INTERVAL_MS 20
 
 /* High quality quality setting @ 44.1 khz */
-#define A2DP_SBC_DEFAULT_BITRATE 328
+#define A2DP_SBC_DEFAULT_BITRATE 229
 
 /*
  * SBC Dual Channel (SBC HD) 3DH5 bitrates.
-- 
2.43.0

